cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite Underlaid, please cite it as below, and mention the date of the data snapshot you used (shown in the site footer) — the score changes with each pipeline run."
title: "Underlaid: cumulative environmental exposure in Paris and its inner suburbs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dussert
    given-names: Jehanne
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-3247-2180"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JehanneDussert/underlaid"
url: "https://underlaid.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  For 2,752 IRIS neighborhoods across Paris, Hauts-de-Seine,
  Seine-Saint-Denis and Val-de-Marne, counts how many of three exposure
  categories (thermal, air/noise pollution, housing) are simultaneously in
  their metro-wide worst quartile, and sets that count beside residents'
  means to cope (median income, overcrowding, secondary residences),
  measured on a separate axis. Built entirely from French public open
  data; methodology documented in SCORING.md. Code under MIT; the
  published data files are under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
keywords:
  - environmental justice
  - urban heat
  - open data
  - Paris
  - geospatial
  - climate adaptation
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
